    "url": "https://www.tiktok.com/@booksandmentalbreakdowns/video/7697753588361121038",
    "author": "booksandmentalbreakdowns",
    "author_followers": "2139",
    "caption": "|| BookTok Books I Haven't Read || So many books, so little time. My Goodreads TBR keeps growing and growing the longer I'm on TikTok or Bookstagram. I'm not complaining over here. It's just a fact. And one we must all live with as readers. Until someone turns me into a vampire \ud83e\udddb\u200d\u2640\ufe0f or figures out alternate routes to immortality, I am left to the harsh reality that there are books in this world--amazing, wonderful books that I would adore--that I simply won't be able to get to. Some of the ones in this list, however, I already own and can quickly add them to the queue. The list today consists of: \ud83d\udcdaAlchemised by SenLin Yu - Do I own it? Yes! \ud83d\udcdaDungeon Crawler Carl by Matt Dinnamin - Do I own it? No \ud83d\udcdaWhen the Moon Hatched by Sarah A. Parker. - Do I own it? Yes! \ud83d\udcdaAnything by Kristin Hannah - Do I own it? No. \ud83d\udcdaThe Plated Prisoner Series by Raven Kennedy - Do I own it? Yes! But only the first book \ud83d\udcdaThreshing Day by Rebecca Yarros - Do I own it? I DO NOW I am currently taking suggestions as to what else I need to add to my TBR. I said it before, and I'll say it again: buying books and reading books are two *different* hobbies. This might be a concept that only bookworms understand, but this could be a good exercise in tolerance for the general public \ud83d\ude02 \ud83d\udcacWhat are your thoughts on these books? Love them? Hate them? Have them on your TBR too? #booktok #readertok #readersoftiktok #booksbooksbooks #reader #reading #booklover #bookworm #bibliophile #bookcommunity #readerthings #buyingbooks #readingbooks #booktokbooks #popularbooks #toberead #bookbuying #bookshopping #booksbuyingproblem #tbr #tbrlist #tbrcart #bookish #morebooks #bookish #bookrecs #bookrecommendation",
